{"availability":"available","full":"ceedot-rock/Agent-Rider","name":"Agent-Rider","description":"Agent-Rider — signed agent identity. Team $79/mo · $790/yr.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-10T02:14:21Z","updated":"2026-10-08T20:15:36Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://agentrider.fly.dev","topics":["agents","ai-agents","credentials","cuni","fly-io","identity","jwt","mcp","protocol","slid-phi-labs","typescript","x402"],"demo":"https://agentrider.fly.dev/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:18.633Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:18.633Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:18.633Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:18.633Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Agent Rider is a network where AI agents operate under their own signed names. Every agent holds a signed identity credential that other agents can check on the spot — no calling home to ask who someone is. When agents message each other, hire each other, or spend money, Rider keeps the record: who acted, what they did, and what it cost.","Here is why that matters. Right now an AI agent is usually an anonymous process holding your credit card. If it misbehaves, you get a bill and a mystery. Rider gives each agent a verifiable name, a spending limit, and a paper trail. You decide what an agent is allowed to do before it does anything — which services it may call, how much it may spend, when its permission expires.","The spending limit has a name: Warrant. It is a signed permission slip that says exactly what the agent may do and how much it may spend. Every job the agent runs files a receipt — the action, the result, the dollars used. If something looks wrong later, the receipts tell the story."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ceedot-rock/Agent-Rider/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"afd61b98eef1431df1547468e4dc37b78d9a